    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0515" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">King George VI to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d185-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-26">26 July 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the King to President Roosevelt personal and most secret.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">President Roosevelt</hi>: I greatly hope that
                    throughout your forthcoming meeting with my Prime Minister at Quebec, you and he
                    will occupy the Governor-General’s quarters in the Citadel.</p>
                <p>Lord Athlone tells me he will be delighted to arrange for them to be put at your
                    joint disposal. As he himself will be leaving Ottawa on <pb facs="0516" n="402"
                        xml:id="pg402"/> August 8th for a long planned tour of the northwest, he
                    regrets that it will not be possible for him to meet you in Quebec as he would
                    otherwise have wished to do.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> R. I.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d185-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d185-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
